   "canonical": "When a partial value is specified using the assignment notation at initialization, only the fields to be assigned values SHALL be specified.",
   "original": "In particular, when specifying partial values (i.e. setting the value of only a subset of the fields) using the assignment notation, at initialization, only the fields to be assigned values shall be specified.",
